WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.000
LedgerLens helps an accounts-payable reviewer
compare an invoice with its purchase order.

00:05.000 --> 00:10.000
Edited genuine UI stills; saved fictional result.
No new Clocked request.

00:10.000 --> 00:15.000
Decide classifies the invoice. Extract reads
invoice facts and payment terms.

00:15.000 --> 00:21.000
Fill reads the purchase order
and drafts a labelled note.

00:21.000 --> 00:28.000
The saved case passed all thirteen
implemented checks.

00:28.000 --> 00:34.000
Each non-null fact must match an exact source span
inside the correct document.

00:34.000 --> 00:40.000
Our first run returned the right PO values
at duplicate invoice locations.

00:40.000 --> 00:46.000
The application stopped before Fill.
We kept that failure and its credit use.

00:46.000 --> 00:51.000
The revised workflow reads
the two documents separately.

00:51.000 --> 00:57.000
Generated wording needs verification
and cannot change the arithmetic checks.

00:57.000 --> 01:02.000
A person must compare the invoice
and confirm fulfillment.

01:02.000 --> 01:07.000
The audit retains source text, facts,
checks and the original request trace.

01:07.000 --> 01:12.000
A genuine browser download matched
the complete saved review.

01:12.000 --> 01:16.000
Replaying this review
makes no new API request.

01:16.000 --> 01:21.000
Both real attempts: five requests,
twenty-eight free credits, zero paid charge.

01:21.000 --> 01:26.000
One fictional case is verified.
This does not establish general accuracy.

01:26.000 --> 01:30.000
LedgerLens never approves
or sends a payment.
